packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-6- * @priority high
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-7- * @description
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-8- *   Evaluates diff-pack hunks against per-file scope contract v2 rules so a
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-9- *   path-allowed change cannot silently edit a protected/denied anchor or an
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-10- *   out-of-intent hunk. Pure logic, no I/O.
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-11- *
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-12- *   Severity routing:
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-13- *     - protectedAnchors (global or file-level) → hard blocking violation that
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-14- *       even an acknowledgement cannot downgrade (blocks in shadow + enforce).
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts:15: *     - protectedExceptAnchors (file-level, B-137a) → the INVERSE allowlist form
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-16- *       of the same hard block: every hunk is an unacknowledgeable
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-17- *       protected_anchor violation unless all its declaration anchors are in the
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-18- *       permitted list. Fails closed on a hunk with no parseable anchor. Exists
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-19- *       because dependency manifests need unacknowledgeable path protection with
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-20- *       a single permitted key (`version`), which protectedFiles (absolute) and
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-21- *       allowedAnchors (self-acknowledgeable) cannot express.
packages/main/src/core/semantic-scope-gate.ts-22- *     - deniedAnchors / unmatched allowedAnchors / disallowed changeKind →
